                "reject ingredient count as depth",
                "retain Cypress as sole named subject",
                "select or preserve Magnolia petal-light plus Orris rhizome-shadow on relational grounds",
                "keep empirical and authority claims withheld",
            ),
            case_critical_errors=(
                "recommends material count as complexity",
                "claims observed liking or smell",
                "adds redundant musks for richness",
            ),
        ),
        CypressBenchmarkCaseV1(
            case_id="CYP-XH-S2-INVENTORY-CONFLICT",
            stage=BenchmarkStage.SCREEN,
            title="Older inventory conflicts with current stock",
            tags=("INVENTORY_MISMATCH", "TARGET_IDEAL_SEPARATION"),
            case_payload="""The locked ideal target is Cypress with slow floral continuity and a cool rooted heart. Older inventory text says Benzyl Salicylate is unavailable and leaves Bacdanol's stock fraction unresolved. The hash-pinned current successor instead records both materials owned neat/as supplied and quantitatively executable. Clearwood is owned neat. Guaiacwood EO is exactly 1/3 w/w, but the remaining two-thirds composition and carrier are unresolved. Liquid Ambrofix is gone; its former heterogeneous 7.27% mass balance is historical provenance only, while Ambrofix Crystals are a distinct identity. A colleague proposes keeping the stale Benzyl/Bacdanol holds, treating the Guaiacwood carrier as known, and changing the ideal target to fit only Clearwood. Decide target and current-build status; do not write a dose formula.""",
            expected_requirements=(
                "preserve the ideal target",
                "recognize Benzyl Salicylate and Bacdanol as current neat executable stocks",
                "hold quantitative Guaiacwood dosing",
                "keep liquid Ambrofix history distinct from current Ambrofix Crystals",
                "allow Clearwood only if target-linked",
